{"hash": "d9847a6662d76ca3", "text": "Re-sending the whole desk is slow and expensive, so providers keep it warm. With prompt caching, the provider stores the work it did reading the start of your request, the prefix, and reuses it when the next request starts exactly the same way. Order matters: tools first, then the system prompt, then the messages. Change anything near the top, and everything below it is laid out again from scratch. The layout sits under a timer, its time to live. Five minutes by default, or an hour at a higher price, and every reuse resets the clock. Claude Code keeps it an hour on a subscription, and five minutes on an A P I key. Take a longer break, and your next message rebuilds the whole desk. Other things break it too: switching models, changing tools, dropping old images, compaction, and on older models, effort. Editing Claude dot M D doesn't; the edit waits for your next session. The cache isn't the clerk remembering. It's stored arithmetic, thrown away when the timer runs out.", "alignment": {"characters": ["R", "e", "-", "s", "e", "n", "d", "i", "n", "g", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "h", "o", "l", "e", " ", "d", "e", "s", "k", " ", "i", "s", " ", "s", "l", "o", "w", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "e", "x", "p", "e", "n", "s", "i", "v", "e", ",", " ", "s", "o", " ", "p", "r", "o", "v", "i", "d", "e", "r", "s", " ", "k", "e", "e", "p", " ", "i", "t", " ", "w", "a", "r", "m", ".", " ", "W", "i", "t", "h", " ", "p", "r", "o", "m", "p", "t", " ", "c", "a", "c", "h", "i", "n", "g", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "r", "o", "v", "i", "d", "e", "r", " ", "s", "t", "o", "r", "e", "s", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "w", "o", "r", "k", " ", "i", "t", " ", "d", "i", "d", " ", "r", "e", "a", "d", "i", "n", "g", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "t", "a", "r", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "r", "e", "q", "u", "e", "s", "t", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "r", "e", "f", "i", "x", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "r", "e", "u", "s", "e", "s"